meta {
  name: 1 List notifications
  type: http
  seq: 1
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/notifications?limit=50&unreadOnly=false
  body: none
}
params:query {
  limit: 50
  unreadOnly: false
}
docs {
  The caller's own inbox, **newest first**, scoped to the `NameIdentifier` claim — there is no address
  in the request, so nothing here can be pointed at somebody else's list.

  `limit` is **clamped, never rejected** (ADR-023): 1–200, defaulting to 50. `limit=0` or a negative
  value gets the default; `limit=100000` gets 200. `unreadOnly=true` drops read rows in the database
  rather than in the client.

  The body is a `NotificationEntity` array — `id`, `recipientEmail`, `subject`, `body`, `type`,
  `appointmentIdentifier`, `createdAt`, `isRead`. ⚠️ `type` is the **integer** of
  `NotificationType`: 0 Booked · 1 Updated · 2 Cancelled · 3 Completed · 4 PasswordResetRequested ·
  5 EmailConfirmationRequested · 6 Requested · 7 MessageReceived. The enum is append-only because the
  integer is what is persisted.
}
